From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 01:33:36 -0400
Subject: accept a tab dragged onto a Space, behind a flag that is off

The reference moves a tab between Spaces by dragging it onto the Space's icon.
This implements that against TabDragTarget, which is the interface Chromium
already resolves through BrowserView::GetTabDragTarget, and it is off.

It is off because it cannot be verified here. A drag needs a pointer, and this
project checks its UI by screenshotting a window it never touches. HandleTabDrop
takes ownership of the dragged tab and is responsible for putting it somewhere;
get that wrong and the tab is gone. Shipping that on the strength of "it
compiles" is not a trade worth making, and the context menu on a Space already
does the same job and is what ships.

To try it:

  tooling/capture-ui --features \
    'SteddingArcStyleWindow:drag_tabs_to_spaces/true'

What it does when on: the tab is detached and put straight back into the same
tab strip, because a Space is not another window -- the tab has not gone
anywhere, it has only changed which Space shows it -- and the target Space
becomes active so the tab stays in front of the user.

Why: it is the last behaviour where this project differs from the reference.
Removable when: it has been driven by a real drag and turned on, or replaced by
something better.
